# Machine-compared files check out with LF endings on every platform.
# tests/lint-ratchet.test.ts demands a byte-identical rewrite of the
# baseline; a CRLF checkout breaks that comparison on Windows.
eslint-baseline.json text eol=lf

# CHANGELOG.md: sequential PRs both append an entry at the same anchor (top of
# [Unreleased] Fixed), so every second PR merge hit a hand-merge conflict
# (#643 against #642's entry, #654 against #653's). The union merge driver
# keeps both sides' lines instead of conflicting — proven on two scratch
# branches: the same two-append merge that read CONFLICT without the driver
# resolves clean with it, both entries kept. Cost: union's line order is
# "ours then theirs", so a merged-in entry can sit below an older one until a
# docs commit tidies it. NEVER extend union to source or test files — it
# duplicates lines on any non-append overlap.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
